Ladybird now treats a replaced grid item’s automatic height as
auto for its minimum contribution, even when that height comes from
its width through its aspect ratio. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79,
Firefox 151.0, and Playwright’s WebKit 26.5, all three engines make
the row in the test 207px.

Blink’s CalculateIntrinsicMinimumContribution() decides from the
computed height, so “height: auto” takes the minimum from min-height.
WebKit’s GridTrackSizingAlgorithmStrategy::minContributionForGridItem()
and Gecko’s CachedIntrinsicSizes::EnsureContributions() decide
from the computed preferred size the same way. WebKit’s RenderBox::
computeMinMaxLogicalHeightFromAspectRatio() and Gecko’s nsLayoutUtils::
IntrinsicForAxis() resolve percentage opposite-axis limits against
the grid area before transferring them through the ratio, which the
transferred size suggestion now does too.
